1452-4    The RT–invariants of the Seifert 3–manifolds
1453-
1454-In this section we will use Corollary 2.7 together with results in [17] to derive
1455-expressions for the quantum g–invariants of all Seifert manifolds, g being an
1456-arbitrary complex finite dimensional simple Lie algebra. The formulas for the
1457-invariants will be expressed in terms of the Seifert invariants together with
1458-
1459-                                               24
1460-standard data for g.
1461-
1462-The RT–invariants of the Seifert manifolds for modular categories
1463-Let us first give some preliminary remarks on modular categories. We use
1464-notation as in [52]. Let (V, {Vi }i∈I ) be an arbitrary modular category with
1465-braiding c and twist θ . The ground ring is K = EndV (I), where I is the unit
1466-object. Let i 7→ i∗ be the involution in I determined by the condition that Vi∗
1467-is isomorphic to the dual of Vi . An element i ∈ I is called self-dual if i = i∗ .
1468-For such an element we have a K –module isomorphism HomV (V ⊗ V, I) ∼       = K,
1469-V = Vi . The map x 7→ x(idV ⊗ θV )cV,V is a K –module endomorphism of
1470-HomV (V ⊗ V, I), so is a multiplication by a certain εi ∈ K . By the definition
1471-of the braiding and twist we have (εi )2 = 1. In particular εi ∈ {±1} if K is a
1472-field. We have a distinguished element 0 ∈ I such that V0 = I.
1473-The S – and T –matrices of V are the matrices S = (Sij )i,j∈I , T = (Tij )i,j∈I
1474-given by Sij = tr(cVj ,Vi ◦ cVi ,Vj ) and Tij = δij vi , where tr is the categorical
1475-trace of V , δij is the Kronecher delta equal to 1 if i = j and zero elsewhere,
1476-and vi ∈ K such that θVi = vi idVi .
1477-Assume that V has a rank D, i.e. an element of K satisfying
1478-                                  X
1479-                           D2 =        dim(i)2 ,
1480-                                          i∈I
1481-
1482-where dim(i) = dim(Vi ) = tr(idVi ). We let
