2758:The asymptotic expansion conjecture and lens spaces In this section
2759:we calculate the large r asymptotics of r 7→ τrg(L(p, q)), r = mκ. Let us
2760-begin by some introductory remarks. Therefore, let X be an arbitrary closed
2761-oriented 3–manifold and let G be a simply connected compact simple Lie group
2762-with complexified Lie algebra g. We are interested in the behaviour of the
2763-complex function κ 7→ τrg(X) in the limit of large κ, i.e. κ → ∞. It is believed
2764-that Witten’s TQFT associated with G and k coincides with the TQFT of
2765-
2766-                                          44
2767-Reshetikhin and Turaev associated with g and k + h∨ . In particular it is
2768-conjectured that Witten’s semiclassical approximation for ZkG (X) should be
2769-valid for the function κ 7→ τrg(X), and furthermore that this function should
2770-have a full asymptotic expansion in the limit κ → ∞. The precise formulation
2771-of this is stated in the following conjecture, called the asymptotic expansion
2772-conjecture (AEC).
2773-
2774-Conjecture 5.4 (J. E. Andersen [1], [2]) Let {α1 , . . . , αM } be the set of
2775-values of the Chern–Simons functional of flat G connections on a closed oriented
2776-                                                                               (j)
