2791-
2792-Here f (κ) = o(κd−N ) means as usual that f (κ)/κd−N → 0 as κ → ∞. The
2793-AEC was proposed by Andersen in [1], where he proved it for the mapping tori
2794-of finite order diffeomorphisms of orientable surfaces of genus at least 2 and for
2795-general g using the gauge theoretic approach to the quantum invariants. These
2796-manifolds are Seifert manifolds with orientable base and Seifert Euler number
2797-equal to zero, see [1, Sect. 4]. NoteP that the semiclassical approximation is
2798-given by putting N = 0 in the sum M     j=1 ... in (36). This part of the AEC and
2799-some of the conjectures concerning the topological interpretation of the different
2800-parts of the asymptotic formula, see [2] for details, are in fact inspired by the
2801-works of Witten, Freed and Gompf, Jeffrey and Rozansky on the semiclassical
2802-approximation of Witten’s invariants.
2803-As already stated, Jeffrey [25], [26] and Garoufalidis [14] made completely rig-
2804-orous calculations of the semiclassical approximation of the SU (2)–invariants
2805:of lens spaces. Actually these calculations contain a complete verification of
2806:the AEC for the lens spaces and g = sl2 (C). Jeffrey’s calculations also contain
2807-a proof of the AEC for a certain class of mapping tori over the torus for an
2808-arbitrary complex finite dimensional simple Lie algebra.
2809-In [46], [47] L. Rozansky calculated the Witten SU (2)–invariants of all Seifert
2810-manifolds with orientable base and carried through a rather technical analy-
2811-sis leading to a candidate for the full asymptotic expansion of these invariants
2812-(for the Seifert manifolds with Seifert Euler number different from zero). As
2813-shown in [17, Sect. 8] the invariants calculated by Rozansky are equal to the
2814-
2815-                                        45
2816-RT–invariants associated to sl2 (C). However, to actually prove that his for-
2817-mula gives the asymptotic expansion of the invariants one has to incorporate
2818-estimations of error terms in the calculations. This was left out in Rozansky’s
2819-calculations. In [16], [18] the first author has supplemented the calculations
2820-of Rozansky by making the necessary error estimates thereby proving, that
2821-Rozansky’s formula is really the asymptotic expansion of these invariants. In
2822-[18] the calculations are carried through for a big class of functions including the
2823-sl2 (C)–invariants of all oriented Seifert manifolds with orientable base or non-
2824-orientable base with even genus (also the ones with Seifert Euler number equal
2825-to zero). Based on results of D. Auckly [5] the Chern–Simons invariants can be
2826-identified in the asymptotic formula thereby proving the AEC, Conjecture 5.4,
2827-for these Seifert manifolds and g = sl2 (C). It should be mentioned that Rozan-
2828-sky and Lawrence have calculated the asymptotics of the sl2 (C)–invariants of
2829-a subclass of the Seifert manifolds with base S 2 by a method which avoids the
2830-rather technical analysis of error terms, cf. [33]. However, it seems that their
2831-method does not work for arbitrary oriented Seifert manifolds.
