3099-In the case of surgery on arbitrary closed oriented 3–manifolds along framed
3100-links we do not have a preferred framing as in the case of surgery on S 3 (or
3101-on another integral homology sphere), i.e. we can not identify the framing of a
3102-link component with an integer in a canonical way, see [17, Appendix B]. Here,
3103-by a framed link in a closed oriented 3–manifold M , we mean a pair (L, Q),
3104-where Q = ∐ni=1 Qi : ∐ni=1 (B 2 × S 1 ) → M is an embedding (or more precisely
3105-an isotopy class of such embeddings) and L is the image by Q of ∐ni=1 (0 × S 1 ).
3106-For other definitions of framed links in 3–manifolds and how these relate to
3107-this definition we refer to [17, Appendix B]. The following result is sensitive to
3108-a choice of orientations. We will use the following conventions.
