3374-In the proof of the main Lemma 2.4, the reciprocity formula, Proposition 2.2, played a
3375-crucial role. The idea of using the reciprocity formula stems from Jeffrey’s calculations
3376-in [25], [26] as already stated in the introduction. Jeffrey’s proof of the reciprocity
3377-formula, which is a verbatim generalization of the argument presented in the proof of
3378-[12, Chap. IX Theorem 1] can be found in her thesis [25].
3379-
3380-In this appendix we will first sketch Jeffrey’s proof, which builds on a limiting case of
3381-the Poisson summation formula applied to Gaussian functions. A main ingredient is the
3382-Fourier transformation of a Gaussian function, which rely on an analytic continuation
3383-argument for complex functions of several variables. Next we will present a slightly
3384-different argument which avoids the direct use of this Fourier transform result.
